        "Michael Berry"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Geometric and topological phases exposed a fundamental, widely applicable structure of quantum mechanics with consequences throughout condensed matter and wave physics.",
        "attribution": "Aharonov's effect established the physical significance of electromagnetic potentials, and Berry identified the general adiabatic geometric phase.",
        "maturity": "Both effects are extensively verified and have become standard conceptual tools, including in modern topological matter.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The two phenomena are historically distinct enough that their treatment as one prize requires a broad unifying formulation."
        ]
      }
    },
