        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks transformed precision measurement by combining confinement-induced control with exceptional frequency accuracy.",
        "attribution": "Katori introduced the magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept, and Ye made foundational experimental and metrological advances.",
        "maturity": "Performance near 10^-18 is established, with major consequences for timekeeping, relativity tests, and geodesy.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The eventual impact on a redefinition of the second and on applications is still evolving."
        ]
      }
